  "title": "Good Edge Labelings",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Question What is the maximum edge density of a graph which has a good edge labeling?\n\nWe say that a graph is good-edge-labeling critical, if it has no good edge labeling, but every proper subgraph has a good edge labeling.\n\nConjecture For every $c<4$, there is only a finite number of good-edge-labeling critical graphs with average degree less than $c$.",
